Hi

I am trying to follow the tutorials from the NicheMapR website and vignettes from the microclima publications:

longlatex <- c(-89.40, 43.07)
dstart <- "01/01/2017"
dfinish <- "31/12/2017"
micro <- micro_ncep(loc = longlatex, dstart = dstart, dfinish = dfinish)

When I run the micro_ncep function, it runs until "computing radiation and elevation effects with package microclima", then I get the following error

Error in microclima::microclimaforNMR(lat = longlat[2], long = longlat[1],  :
  unused arguments (weather.elev = weather.elev, cad.effects = cad.effects)

I get the same error for whatever inputs I change weather.elev and cad.effects to.
The same error occurs if I use runauto from microclima, and whether I use longlatex or the co-ordinates as the argument for loc.

